WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:09.175
[ominous music playing]

2
00:00:09.176 --> 00:00:11.345
[tools grinding. whirring]

3
00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:56.013
You said you knew where she was going.

4
00:00:56.014 --> 00:00:59.517
- I did. She got away.
- From you.

5
00:00:59.518 --> 00:01:02.061
She was helped
by one of her Mechanical friends.

6
00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.604
I chased them.
but they got down here first

7
00:01:04.605 --> 00:01:07.067
and disappeared
before I could get a chair.

8
00:01:09.027 --> 00:01:10.821
You already knew I was down here.

9
00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:15.492
People take notice
of where you go. Robert.

10
00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:18.328
You know what?
I'll-I'll take it from here.

11
00:01:18.996 --> 00:01:21.205
I know Greasetown. And it's still on edge.

12
00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:23.207
I've got Jo and Chad.
I think I can manage.

13
00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:24.751
I should be here for you.

14
00:01:26.128 --> 00:01:27.880
- We could split up.
- Go home to Anthony.

15
00:01:29.882 --> 00:01:31.175
Spend time with him.

16
00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:34.135
It doesn't have to come to that.

17
00:01:34.136 --> 00:01:36.221
It will if I can't find her.

18
00:01:43.562 --> 00:01:46.230
Camille Sims for Emerson.
I'm below the gap.

19
00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:48.024
When Nichols was a fugitive.
she was caught down here.

20
00:01:48.025 --> 00:01:49.150
Find out where.

21
00:01:49.151 --> 00:01:50.903
Oh. and Judge Sims is headed up.

22
00:01:51.612 --> 00:01:52.905
Keep eyes on himâ€¦

23
00:01:53.572 --> 00:01:55.657
- for his safety.
- [Emerson] <i>Copy that</i>.

24
00:01:57.951 --> 00:02:01.829
[Bernard breathing heavily]

25
00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:04.583
[groans] I need to lie down.

26
00:02:06.001 --> 00:02:07.961
[grunts] Have some water.

27
00:02:08.544 --> 00:02:12.424
The actual fuck? You're alive?

28
00:02:13.175 --> 00:02:14.426
He's alive?

29
00:02:21.016 --> 00:02:22.267
- [Bernard sighs]
- Here.

30
00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:26.104
Anybody else coming back from the dead?

31
00:02:26.647 --> 00:02:28.148
The old sheriff. maybe his wife?

32
00:02:29.107 --> 00:02:30.442
Did anybody see you?

33
00:02:31.777 --> 00:02:33.277
Just Teddy.

34
00:02:33.278 --> 00:02:34.780
[gulps. sighs]

35
00:02:35.614 --> 00:02:36.865
Mr. Kyle.

36
00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:38.909
Mr. Holland.

37
00:02:39.743 --> 00:02:43.330
I'm very glad you're still alive.

38
00:02:44.373 --> 00:02:45.374
[scoffs]

39
00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.753
I didn't think you'd survive the move.

40
00:02:50.754 --> 00:02:54.924
Isn't there a small part of you
that's happy to see me again?

41
00:02:54.925 --> 00:02:55.926
[door opens]

42
00:03:00.973 --> 00:03:04.852
[pants] I remember.
I know what we have to do.

43
00:03:09.064 --> 00:03:10.607
<i>Emerson for Camille Sims</i>.

44
00:03:11.859 --> 00:03:13.776
- Go.
- The address you were looking for

45
00:03:13.777 --> 00:03:17.698
is a workshop on 144.
occupied by Martha Walker.

46
00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.538
One of the lines must have been a pipe.

47
00:03:26.373 --> 00:03:27.456
What?

48
00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:32.044
Mr. Kyle put the hard drive I smashed
back together.

49
00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.505
The-The diagram you found

50
00:03:34.506 --> 00:03:38.217
showed lines coming in from outside.

51
00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:42.138
There are two lines. One goes to IT.
and the other goes to Judicial.

52
00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:43.723
And I didn't know what the lines were.

53
00:03:43.724 --> 00:03:45.474
but that's why I went to the mines.

54
00:03:45.475 --> 00:03:46.684
[Kennedy] Yeah. well. you're an idiot.

55
00:03:46.685 --> 00:03:49.979
They're not gonna put some killer pipe
where criminals dig all day.

56
00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.024
There are tunnels in the mines
that go up and down the Silo.

57
00:03:53.025 --> 00:03:55.359
And I almost made it
to the line that goes into IT

58
00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.694
when they gassed the mines.

59
00:03:56.695 --> 00:04:01.992
The lines going into IT
carry electricity from Silo 1.

60
00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:07.079
So if the generator stops
there's always power in IT.

61
00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:12.376
So. then the line that goes to Judicial.
th-that's the Safeguard.

62
00:04:12.377 --> 00:04:14.504
I think that's what he said. That'sâ€¦

63
00:04:14.505 --> 00:04:16.547
- I think that's what Jimmy said.
- Now hold on. who is Jimmy?

64
00:04:16.548 --> 00:04:18.549
Jimmy is the guy that I was with in 17.

65
00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:20.218
That's whatâ€¦ I think that's what he said.

66
00:04:20.219 --> 00:04:25.891
Did this Jimmy tell you
where the lines entered into Judicial?

67
00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:31.230
[Juliette] <i>He had an old blueprint. butâ€¦</i>

68
00:04:36.777 --> 00:04:39.947
No. Itâ€¦ I can'tâ€¦ [stammering] It's gone.

69
00:04:54.336 --> 00:04:55.920
Where's our blueprint?

70
00:04:55.921 --> 00:04:58.631
Look. if we have a blueprint.
it would be on that hard drive

71
00:04:58.632 --> 00:04:59.799
which is back in IT.

72
00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.467
We're not gonna get to that.

73
00:05:01.468 --> 00:05:04.554
Well. maybe your new pal. Sims.
can help us find it.

74
00:05:04.555 --> 00:05:05.805
Where is Sims?

75
00:05:05.806 --> 00:05:07.098
He went to head off Camille.

76
00:05:07.099 --> 00:05:10.226
Wait. Is 17 the same as our silo?

77
00:05:10.227 --> 00:05:11.894
Yeah. they're exactly the same.

78
00:05:11.895 --> 00:05:15.439
So. then if we find the pipe in 17.
we find it here.

79
00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.733
Is there a way to communicate with Jimmy?

80
00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:20.695
Every silo has its own frequency.
so I can try to--

81
00:05:20.696 --> 00:05:24.449
I never saw him with a radio.
I never found a radio. I--

82
00:05:25.075 --> 00:05:26.909
Camille Sims is coming this way.

83
00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:27.994
[Bernard] Oh. shit.

84
00:05:27.995 --> 00:05:30.163
- We're gonna have to move you again.
- [grunts]

85
00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:33.166
- Go.
- Shit.

86
00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.253
[Hank] You serious?

87
00:05:37.254 --> 00:05:38.713
How long do we have?

88
00:05:38.714 --> 00:05:40.756
[Paul] McLain said
when she became Head of Supply

89
00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:43.676
we had 70 years of light bulbs left.

90
00:05:43.677 --> 00:05:46.805
Since someone started stealing them.
it's down to two.

91
00:05:50.559 --> 00:05:51.810
What do we do?

92
00:05:53.812 --> 00:05:56.480
First. we keep this to ourselves.

93
00:05:56.481 --> 00:05:58.441
It's only been three months
since one rebellion.

94
00:05:58.442 --> 00:05:59.651
we can't have another one.

95
00:06:00.986 --> 00:06:03.238
Then we find out who killed Orla Kent.

96
00:06:03.906 --> 00:06:07.158
When we do. we might find out
who stole the light bulbs.

97
00:06:07.159 --> 00:06:09.994
Or if we find out who's
been stealing light bulbs.

98
00:06:09.995 --> 00:06:12.039
maybe we find out who killed Orla Kent.

99
00:06:15.209 --> 00:06:16.793
[tense music plays]

100
00:06:38.649 --> 00:06:40.317
Before you arrest me. we should talk.

101
00:06:41.318 --> 00:06:42.736
Somewhere with no cameras.

102
00:06:45.239 --> 00:06:48.158
[whispers] I remember everything.

103
00:08:49.905 --> 00:08:51.864
- Oh. fuck.
- Fuck what?

104
00:08:51.865 --> 00:08:53.366
[stammers] We're now going 70.

105
00:08:53.367 --> 00:08:55.826
We probably should have tried to jump out
when we were still in the city.

106
00:08:55.827 --> 00:08:59.038
I said that. and then you said
that we would die even at 40.

107
00:08:59.039 --> 00:09:00.540
Only horribly injured.

108
00:09:00.541 --> 00:09:03.084
But now. we'd definitely just be a smear.

109
00:09:03.085 --> 00:09:05.795
Can you justâ€¦ Can you just try
taking out the key? Please.

110
00:09:05.796 --> 00:09:06.797
No.

111
00:09:12.177 --> 00:09:14.428
- Hey. What?
- If we get the fob away from the van.

112
00:09:14.429 --> 00:09:17.181
- won't it just stop working?
- I hope not.

113
00:09:17.182 --> 00:09:19.810
Your kid tosses it.
and you shut down in the middle of I-95?

114
00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:21.394
Not safe.

115
00:09:21.395 --> 00:09:24.355
Safe is not what
I'm fucking feeling right now.

116
00:09:24.356 --> 00:09:26.399
[sighs] No brakes. No steering.

117
00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.693
This is like what
happened to Charlotte's squadron.

118
00:09:28.694 --> 00:09:30.611
You think someone in Iran is driving this?

119
00:09:30.612 --> 00:09:31.905
I don't know. but someone is.

120
00:09:33.323 --> 00:09:37.285
Stensen's been sounding the alarm
on how AI can be used by hackers. right?

121
00:09:37.286 --> 00:09:38.703
So maybe he was on the <i>Nimitz</i>

122
00:09:38.704 --> 00:09:41.290
because he feared
the planes would be compromised.

123
00:09:41.832 --> 00:09:43.083
And they were.

124
00:09:44.585 --> 00:09:45.794
Too crazy?

125
00:09:47.171 --> 00:09:48.921
[sighs] I think we're neck-deep in crazy.

126
00:09:48.922 --> 00:09:49.923
[sighs]

127
00:09:52.593 --> 00:09:54.928
I need something with a flat edge.

128
00:10:03.395 --> 00:10:04.396
[Helen] Damn it.

129
00:10:14.573 --> 00:10:15.616
Uh. [sighs]

130
00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:17.701
Here.

131
00:10:32.007 --> 00:10:33.549
[breathing heavily]

132
00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:35.385
- Do you actually know what you're doing?
- [exhales sharply]

133
00:10:35.928 --> 00:10:38.222
Uh. roughly. Brakes are simple.

134
00:10:38.722 --> 00:10:44.310
You step on a pedal. it activates a line
which makes the brake pads squeeze.

135
00:10:44.311 --> 00:10:46.187
But whoever'sâ€¦ [stammers] â€¦driving this.

136
00:10:46.188 --> 00:10:48.689
is doing something
with the electronics to stop that.

137
00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:50.441
So. if I can access theâ€¦ [grunts]

138
00:10:50.442 --> 00:10:51.527
- What?
- Fuck!

139
00:10:52.277 --> 00:10:53.403
[breathes heavily]

140
00:10:54.196 --> 00:10:55.363
Damn it.

141
00:10:55.364 --> 00:10:56.615
Oh.

142
00:11:01.119 --> 00:11:02.120
Let me see.

143
00:11:14.091 --> 00:11:15.300
Think you'll live?

144
00:11:16.134 --> 00:11:17.135
Sure hope so.

145
00:11:24.852 --> 00:11:26.186
I know about the voice.

146
00:11:27.771 --> 00:11:29.398
- What voice?
- No. don't do that.

147
00:11:30.983 --> 00:11:32.818
I'm not gonna talk to you about this.

148
00:11:34.069 --> 00:11:36.655
Camille. you know I didn't go
into a refuge hut.

149
00:11:37.281 --> 00:11:41.410
I don't know what it tells you.
but I went into another silo.

150
00:11:42.661 --> 00:11:43.995
Hmm.

151
00:11:43.996 --> 00:11:46.748
It's not dead. There are kids in it.

152
00:11:47.291 --> 00:11:49.959
And they're alone. and somehow
they've managed to survive.

153
00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:52.336
But I promised them
that I would go back to them.

154
00:11:52.337 --> 00:11:53.963
That's what I remember.

155
00:11:53.964 --> 00:11:56.549
I remember that I said
I would bring them back here.

156
00:11:56.550 --> 00:12:00.720
- That's an insane request.
- Let me ask the voice. and it can decide.

157
00:12:00.721 --> 00:12:01.763
No.

158
00:12:04.933 --> 00:12:07.144
You know people treat me
like a living Founder.

159
00:12:07.769 --> 00:12:09.563
If I jump off the stairs. they'll follow.

160
00:12:11.064 --> 00:12:12.816
You wanna see what else
they're willing to do for me?

161
00:12:13.483 --> 00:12:15.735
You sound like a threat to the Silo.

162
00:12:15.736 --> 00:12:20.449
No. Camille. I want to save the kids.

163
00:12:23.076 --> 00:12:24.786
[device buzzing]

164
00:12:28.165 --> 00:12:31.084
You sure there are no cameras here?
It looks like it knows we're talking.

165
00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:32.711
[buzzing continues]

166
00:12:44.389 --> 00:12:46.308
- Any luck?
- No.

167
00:12:47.392 --> 00:12:49.603
[sighs] There has to be some way
to stop this thing.

168
00:12:52.231 --> 00:12:53.690
- Oh. oh!
- What?

169
00:12:54.650 --> 00:12:59.195
Hey. hey. hey. hey. hey!
Hey! Stop! Call the police!

170
00:12:59.196 --> 00:13:01.615
Help. help. help. help!
Stop. stop. stop. stop!

171
00:13:02.199 --> 00:13:07.037
Please. please. please!
Call the police! Stop! Hey!

172
00:13:10.165 --> 00:13:11.333
What the fuck?

173
00:13:13.126 --> 00:13:14.378
What happened?

174
00:13:17.714 --> 00:13:19.216
I think I know how to stop this thing.

175
00:13:20.926 --> 00:13:24.178
Hank. I make things. I don't steal them.

176
00:13:24.179 --> 00:13:26.389
We're just hoping
you know somebody who does.

177
00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:29.892
I only associate
with Pact-abiding citizens. you know that.

178
00:13:29.893 --> 00:13:33.688
Mark. weâ€¦ we've got something
pretty serious going on.

179
00:13:33.689 --> 00:13:35.398
We could really use your help.

180
00:13:35.399 --> 00:13:38.359
Serious. like getting chucked
over the rail?

181
00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:41.737
There are two raiders guilty of throwing
my best friend to his death

182
00:13:41.738 --> 00:13:43.322
during the rebellion.

183
00:13:43.323 --> 00:13:45.533
But I don't hear you asking about that.

184
00:13:45.534 --> 00:13:49.371
This friend of yours.
was his name Lee Torgenson?

185
00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.915
And was he thrown over
for using a weapon you made for him?

186
00:13:52.916 --> 00:13:55.627
- Oh. fuck you. Who the fuck are you?
- I'm the sheriff.

187
00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:58.379
- And if you don't cooperate. we--
- You're not a sheriff.

188
00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:00.173
- You're an accident.
- [Hank] Mark.

189
00:14:00.174 --> 00:14:01.424
You got the job by default.

190
00:14:01.425 --> 00:14:03.843
Now you're standing here
wearing Holston's hand-me-downs.

191
00:14:03.844 --> 00:14:05.761
and they're one size too big.

192
00:14:05.762 --> 00:14:07.096
You wanna arrest someone?

193
00:14:07.097 --> 00:14:08.848
- Arrest your wife.
- Mark!

194
00:14:08.849 --> 00:14:11.225
You think people don't know
about her and the Outsiders?

195
00:14:11.226 --> 00:14:13.019
Trying to get us all killed?

196
00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:16.064
Oh. What are you going to do. Mr. Sheriff?
Drag me out of here?

197
00:14:16.857 --> 00:14:18.108
That'll look great.

198
00:14:21.486 --> 00:14:22.946
[Hank] Mark. we are not threatening you.

199
00:14:23.572 --> 00:14:26.073
We're just in a tough spot.
and we really need to know

200
00:14:26.074 --> 00:14:29.952
if anyone has info on things
disappearing from Critical Supply.

201
00:14:29.953 --> 00:14:32.456
I'm not doing shit for this asshole.

202
00:14:37.794 --> 00:14:39.213
How about thisâ€¦

203
00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:45.052
You give us something we can use.
and I'll look into the raiders.

204
00:14:46.178 --> 00:14:47.929
- You won't do anything--
- I'll get their names.

205
00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:51.767
I'll give them to you. Whatever you do
with that information is up to you.

206
00:15:05.113 --> 00:15:06.114
All right.

207
00:15:08.158 --> 00:15:12.663
Here's thisâ€¦
The weapons I made. I made for Knox.

208
00:15:13.247 --> 00:15:15.082
You wanna know about stolen shit?

209
00:15:16.416 --> 00:15:18.460
His father was crooked as a screw.

210
00:15:19.419 --> 00:15:21.420
He used to steal
diamond drill bits from Supply.

211
00:15:21.421 --> 00:15:23.173
and sold 'em on the black market
as jewelry.

212
00:15:23.924 --> 00:15:25.676
Far as I know. he's out of that game.

213
00:15:26.426 --> 00:15:28.136
But he'll know more than I will.

214
00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.264
That something you can use?

215
00:15:36.436 --> 00:15:37.604
Get me those names.

216
00:15:39.523 --> 00:15:41.233
- You all right?
- I'm fine.

217
00:15:52.953 --> 00:15:55.414
[Helen] We just sit. and we wait. [sighs]

218
00:15:56.206 --> 00:15:58.124
Come on. [stammers]
All it takes is one person

219
00:15:58.125 --> 00:16:01.712
to see an empty van driving by itself.
and they will call the cops.

220
00:16:04.798 --> 00:16:07.384
Oh. ye of little faith.

221
00:16:08.927 --> 00:16:10.220
[device chimes]

222
00:16:20.189 --> 00:16:21.523
[door closes]

223
00:16:34.119 --> 00:16:37.456
[The Algorithm]
<i>Juliette Nichols. why are you here?</i>

224
00:16:43.837 --> 00:16:45.005
You just speak.

225
00:16:46.548 --> 00:16:47.841
Okay. Umâ€¦

226
00:16:49.843 --> 00:16:52.054
I know what happened when I went outside.

227
00:16:52.721 --> 00:16:58.143
Andâ€¦ In Silo 17 there are kids.
and I want to bring them back. Here.

228
00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:06.026
Silo 17 is flooding.
a-and they're gonna die.

229
00:17:10.614 --> 00:17:14.785
I'm not working against the Silo.
I'm not working against you.

230
00:17:15.827 --> 00:17:17.204
I'm not a threat.

231
00:17:22.459 --> 00:17:25.586
[The Algorithm] <i>The numbers predict
disaster for the Silo if you leave.</i>

232
00:17:25.587 --> 00:17:27.046
<i>Request is denied.</i>

233
00:17:27.047 --> 00:17:29.841
No. not me.
We'll send someone else to get them.

234
00:17:29.842 --> 00:17:31.300
[The Algorithm]
<i>The numbers predict disaster</i>

235
00:17:31.301 --> 00:17:34.304
<i>if residents from another silo
join Silo 18</i>.

236
00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:36.806
<i>Request is denied</i>.

237
00:17:36.807 --> 00:17:40.143
No. but they're kids.
They're gonna die in 17.

238
00:17:41.895 --> 00:17:45.356
[The Algorithm] <i>They'd be invasive.
Request is denied.</i>

239
00:17:45.357 --> 00:17:47.776
Time to leave. Come on.

240
00:17:54.992 --> 00:17:58.745
Okay. what if I go back on
the memory drug? Is that what you want?

241
00:17:59.872 --> 00:18:01.123
I'll do it.

242
00:18:05.586 --> 00:18:07.838
You can even drug the kids.

243
00:18:10.382 --> 00:18:12.467
And then they won't be a threat
to anyone here. right?

244
00:18:14.386 --> 00:18:15.387
[Juliette breathes shakily]

245
